        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays' season teetered on a knife's edge after a brutal two-game swing in Seattle, exposing a team that can't sustain momentum when the pressure mounts. <strong>The Jays fell to the Mariners 11-0 on July 4</strong>, a humiliation that included a Randy Arozarena grand slam and just one hit off Shane Bieber, pushing them back to five games under.500. Now sitting at 42-47 and 11.5 games behind in the AL East, the Blue Jays are in honest assessment mode - not contender energy. Dylan Cease's franchise-record 137 strikeouts in 16 starts and Vladimir Guerrero Jr. turning down an All-Star invite show individual brilliance, but the team can't convert it into wins. <strong>The final game of the series at 5:00 PM ET today at Mariners is the chance to salvage pride before the All-Star break</strong>.",
